hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18013","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Dawud ibn Abi Hind from Abdullah ibn Qays, he said: I heard al-Harith ibn Uqaysh narrating that Abu Barzah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Indeed among my community are those who will intercede for more than Rabiah and Mudar, and indeed among my community are those who will be magnified for the Fire until he becomes a pillar of its pillars."
"18014","Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us from Dawud from Abdullah ibn Qays from al-Harith ibn Uqaysh, he said: We were with Abu Barzah one night, then that night he narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: There are no two Muslims to whom four predeceased children die except Allah admits them to Paradise by the bounty of His mercy. They said: O Messenger of Allah, and three. He said: And three. They said: And two. He said: And two. He said: And indeed among my community is one who enters Paradise by his intercession like Mudar. He said: And indeed among my community is one who is magnified for the Fire until he becomes one of its corners."
